# core/.lock-state — written by lock-kit.sh's write_state(). It describes the TREE IT SITS IN
# (see install.sh's matching fix), never the repo/pack it happens to be committed from. A
# committed record would travel to every clone or fork, claiming a lock event that never happened
# to THEIR copy — and at "hardened" that reads back as `mismatch` (_integrity.sh's integrity_tier),
# which REFUSES every entrypoint. It has never been committed here; this just makes that permanent.
#
# This file lives under core/ specifically so it ships WITH the kit: install.sh's
# `cp -R "$HERE/core/." "$SKILL_DIR/core/"` carries it into every installed project too, so the
# same protection follows downstream instead of only covering this repo's own copy.
.lock-state
